# Stalked Researcher (3/3 defender), "Eerie - Whenever an enchantment you control enters ..., this creature can attack this turn as though
# it didn't have defender": on turn 3 nothing has entered, so only a Memnite (the positive control, which makes the declaration happen)
# may attack and Stalked Researcher may not; on turn 5 Bot1's Flood enters, the trigger resolves and it attacks with Memnite
# (Bot2 20 -> 19 -> 15); on turn 7 the permission has ended with turn 5, so it may not attack again.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Stalked Researcher
Flood
Memnite
Island
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x27

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Stalked Researcher.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
! Bot1.Attack(Stalked Researcher > Bot2)
Bot1.Attack(Memnite > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Life = 19
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Flood.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Attack(Stalked Researcher; Memnite > Bot2)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Life = 15
[T7 Bot1.Main1]
! Bot1.Attack(Stalked Researcher > Bot2)
Bot1.Attack(Memnite > Bot2)
[T7 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 14
